\begin_layout Standard
Pico 2 W contains an on-board 2.4GHz wireless interface using the Infineon CYW43439,
 which has the following features:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WiFi 4 (802.11n),
 Single-band (2.4 GHz)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WPA3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
SoftAP (Up to 4 clients)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bluetooth 5.2
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Support for Bluetooth LE Central and Peripheral roles
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Support for Bluetooth Classic
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The antenna is an onboard antenna licensed from ABRACON (formerly ProAnt).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The wireless interface is connected via SPI to the RP2350.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Due to pin limitations some of the wireless interface pins are shared.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CLK is shared with VSYS monitor so only when there isn’t an SPI transaction in progress can VSYS be read via the ADC.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Infineon CYW43439 DIN/DOUT and IRQ all share one pin on the RP2350.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Only when an SPI transaction isn’t in progress is it suitable to check for IRQs.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The interface typically runs at 33MHz.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are three GPIO pins from the CYW43439 that are used for other board functions and can easily be accessed via the SDK:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO2
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
IP VBUS sense - high if VBUS is present else low
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO1
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
OP controls the on-board SMPS power save pin (Section 3.4)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
WL_GPIO0
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
OP connected to user LED
\end_layout

